{
 "_readme": "Effect art mapping, carried over from the old Phaser build's src/config/visual-effects.json. Paths are RELATIVE \u2014 the arcade serves this game from /games/fleet-forge/ so the old root-absolute '/images/...' 404s. `scale` is world units per source pixel: a 76px-tall ballistic sprite at 0.015 draws 1.14 units long, which is the size the battle camera expects. `rotationOffset` is added to the projectile's travel angle because every projectile sprite is drawn nose-up. Sheet layouts were re-measured against the actual PNGs, not trusted from the old loader. Sections dropped from the old config and why: `laser` (colours, not art \u2014 beams are one batched stroke and the arcade palette owns their colour), `point_defense` (same), `effects.warp` / `effects.shield_hit` (colours and durations for procedural rings that already exist), `effects.missile_trail` (a Phaser particle-emitter spec; per-missile smoke would swamp a 240-slot pool, so smoke plays on explosions instead), `modules` (ring colours owned by theme.js), the `pellets` / `maxLifetime` keys (the sim owns spread and lifetime), and the `reactor` explosion scale (a reactor going critical raises no event of its own \u2014 it is a `destroy` like any other module). `explosions.ship` is new: the old config had no size for a whole ship dying.",
